VALUES ('Clearly Calendula Evening Tea Benefits', 'clearly-calendula-evening-tea-benefits', '2021-08-31', 'BeauTeas Team', 'What is in our Clearly Calendula Afternoon Tea and just how does it help your skin? Read about all of the wonderful organic ingredients and how they help not just your skin, but your heart, body, and mind!

What is in our Clearly Calendula Evening Tea and just how does it help your skin? Read about all of the wonderful organic ingredients and how they help not just your skin, but your heart, body, and mind!', '[]', 'https://img.beauteas.com/blog/85A6131.jpg', 'Clearly Calendula Evening Tea Benefits',
   'published', '<p>BeauTeas - August 02 2021</p>
<h3>What is our Clearly Calendula Evening tea and how does it work?</h3>
<p>Clearly Calendula Evening is a soothing caffeine free Herbal tea. We start off with chamomile and rooibos. Then we add spearmint, peppermint, and calendula pedals.&nbsp;&nbsp;<br /><br />All of our ingredients are 100% Organic and certified by the USDA! <br /><br />Herbal teas have a mild flavor, don’t get bitter from overstepping, and are a great choice before bed or anytime you want a calming, caffeine free, drink.<br /><br />Let’s talk about all the ways the tea is good for you!</p>
<h3>TLDR;</h3>
<p>This tea is tasty and rich in antioxidants, anti-inflammatories, and lots of things that help prevent acne AND heal and improve your skin! It’s calming and helps you get better sleep. <br /><br />It’s also good for women especially helping reduce cramps, period pain, and hormonal acne.</p>
<h3>Organic Chamomile</h3>
<img src="https://img.beauteas.com/blog/pf-fe04203d--rolandyeghiazaryanXcay0Tq9HNounsplash.jpg" alt="" />
<p>Chamomile tea contains chamazulene, which is an anti-inflammatory, analgesic, and antispasmodic. It’s known for being very calming and relaxing, and is used in many bedtime teas. It not only helps promote sleepiness, but also reduces insomnia. Many studies show that regularly drinking chamomile tea measurably improves the quality of your sleep. Good sleep is critical not only for your mood, energy, and mental health, but also gives your body time to heal and rejuvenate your skin, hair, nails, and whole body!<br /><br />Chamomile boosts your immune system, keeping you healthy and helping fight off colds or other illnesses if you are sick. It has powerful pain relieving properties, and also helps relax the uterus and reduce period pains. It also helps soothe your stomach.<br /><br />Chamomile teas also have anti-microbial properties which help clear up acne, and heal skin damage from psoriasis and eczema. It can eliminate dandruff and scalp irritation, helping your hair look as good as possible. It also helps fade skin spots, heal old acne scars, and smooth your complexion.<br /><br />It is rich in antioxidants, slowing down the signs of aging and preventing sun damage to your skin. It also helps control blood sugar and protects your pancreas, helping prevent diabetes.</p>
<h3>Organic Rooibos</h3>
<img src="https://img.beauteas.com/blog/pf-14fe0420--teacorarooibos8sdQBNAdMOYunsplash.jpg" alt="" />
<p>Rooibos is extremely rich in antioxidants. Antioxidants neutralize free radicals in our bodies. Free radicals are a waste product from cells and build up to create “oxidative stress” in your body. This can cause heart disease, cancer, arthritis, strokes, emphysema, and many other health issues. There’s a ton of research showing how important antioxidants are not just to your long term health, but also to reduce signs of aging in your skin, prevent sun damage, and help your skin heal and glow! We’ll talk about antioxidants a lot as most of our ingredients are rich in antioxidants!<br /><br />&nbsp;Rooibos also contains AHA (Alpha Hydroxy Acid) and zinc, both of which are great for your skin. AHAs promote collagen production and blood flow. They help correct discoloration from age spots and acne scars. They can brighten your complexion and give you the glow you deserve.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>
<h3>Organic Spearmint</h3>
<img src="https://img.beauteas.com/blog/pf-8f73898a--abbyboggierboadZKqd1YMunsplash.jpg" alt="" />
<p>Spearmint has an anti-androgenic effect on women, which reduces acne caused by hormones. It can also reduce facial hair production in women. <br /><br /> It’s very high in antioxidants which we''ve talked about before, helps lower your blood sugar (helping prevent diabetes) and reduces stress.</p>
<h3>Organic Peppermint</h3>
<img src="https://img.beauteas.com/blog/pf-47d69e2c--nelimalubisiawoBIe5TBEpUunsplash.jpg" alt="" />
<p>Peppermint aids in digestion and reduces bloating. It has menthol in it, which reduces oil production in the skin, which in turn helps prevent acne. It’s also rich in vitamins D and E, which both increase cell turnover, helping us shed the outer layer of skin, leaving us with that fresh faced, coveted glow!</p>
<h3>Organic Calendula Petals</h3>
<img src="https://img.beauteas.com/blog/pf-20560b7e--1621315185705iStock1211331956.jpg" alt="" />
<p>The Calendula Flower is the key ingredient in our Clearly Calendula line of teas. You can read all about it here: <a href="/blog/the-magical-calendula-flower ">/blog/the-magical-calendula-flower </a>Calendula has many healing properties, and several of them help clear up your skin and bring out your inner beauty. <br /><br /> It has antiseptic properties, which help treat wounds, including minor skin wounds like acne. It stimulates collagen production, which helps your lips and cheeks look more plump and full. Calendula helps moisturize dry skin, and is great at reducing oily skin, it’s another great anti-inflammatory. The calendula flower boosts the creation of some proteins in your body giving you stronger and healthier hair, nails, and skin!<br /><br />Calendula also helps to relieve menstrual cramps and pain, and generally lessen the discomforts of the menstrual cycle. <br /><br />It really is a powerful flower, which fits perfectly with our mission to help you Build Your Beauty From Within!</p>
<h3><i></i>Try Some! 30 Day Money Back Gaurantee!</h3>
<p>That is it!&nbsp; Five Organic Plants and Flowers. No other ingredients or chemicals. Clean, All Natural, Plant Based, Organic, Beauty!&nbsp; We know you''ll love it, so we offer a 30 day money back guarantee!</p>
<img src="https://img.beauteas.com/blog/pf-1214fe04--85A6695.jpg" alt="" />
<h3>Don''t Take Our Word For It. There is SCIENCE!</h3>
<p><a href="http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0301051106001451?via=ihub">http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0301051106001451?via=ihub</a><br /><a href="http://online.liebertpub.com/doi/abs/10.1089/jmf.2009.1374">http://online.liebertpub.com/doi/abs/10.1089/jmf.2009.1374</a><br /><a href="https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00394-014-0720-1">https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00394-014-0720-1</a><br /><a href="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/24861099">https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/24861099</a><br /><a href="https://www.mcgill.ca/oss/article/health-and-nutrition-quackery/how-make-healthiest-cup-tea">https://www.mcgill.ca/oss/article/health-and-nutrition-quackery/how-make-healthiest-cup-tea</a><br /><a href="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6512146/">https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6512146/</a><br /><a href="http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3249911/">http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3249911/</a><br /><a href="https://www.medicalnewstoday.com/articles/237191.php">https://www.medicalnewstoday.com/articles/237191.php</a><br /><a href="https://www.medicalnewstoday.com/articles/301506">https://www.medicalnewstoday.com/articles/301506</a><br /><a href="https://www.dermstore.com/blog/antioxidants-in-skin-care/">https://www.dermstore.com/blog/antioxidants-in-skin-care/</a><br /><a href="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5514576/">https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5514576/</a><br /><a href="https://www.healthline.com/nutrition/spearmint">https://www.healthline.com/nutrition/spearmint</a><br /><a href="https://durefoods.com/the-benefits-of-vanilla/">https://durefoods.com/the-benefits-of-vanilla/</a><br /><a href="/blog/the-magical-calendula-flower">/blog/the-magical-calendula-flower</a><br /><a href="https://www.list-of-birthstones.com/birth%20flowers/flower-uses/calendula-health-benefits.php">https://www.list-of-birthstones.com/birth%20flowers/flower-uses/calendula-health-benefits.php</a><br /><a href="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3841996/">https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3841996/</a><br /><a href="https://www.medicalnewstoday.com/articles/320031">https://www.medicalnewstoday.com/articles/320031</a><br /><a href="https://www.healthline.com/nutrition/5-benefits-of-chamomile-tea#">https://www.healthline.com/nutrition/5-benefits-of-chamomile-tea#</a><br /><a href="https://food.ndtv.com/food-drinks/13-incredible-chamomile-tea-benefits-drink-up-1629069">https://food.ndtv.com/food-drinks/13-incredible-chamomile-tea-benefits-drink-up-1629069</a><br /><a href="https://www.healthline.com/health/beauty-skin-care/alpha-hydroxy-acid">https://www.healthline.com/health/beauty-skin-care/alpha-hydroxy-acid</a><br /></p>', 4,
